WEBVTT

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.540
"The Vampire of the Blue Moon."

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:25.920
There was once a vampire known as Vanitas,
who was despised by his own kind.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.430
Others of his kind were born
on the night of the crimson moon,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:39.440
but he alone was born under
the blue moon, a sign of ill omen.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.440
The other vampires feared Vanitas
and drove him from the village.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.690
Wandering alone in the woods,

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.860
he faced the terrors of darkness
and the cold clutches of snow.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.410
So it was that he made a vow.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:00.500
He would take vengeance upon vampires
born under the crimson moon.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.250
O foolish vampires who have persecuted me!

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:10.880
Opening this grimoire shall visit
upon you a curse worse than death!

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.390
Vanitas's special creation

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:20.060
was a book that he imbued with the
power to corrupt a vampire's true name.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.270
Those who take my grimoire in hand

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.940
shall, like me, have the blue light
instilled in their eyes,

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.900
and before long, become a bringer
of death upon all vampire kind.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.550
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.310
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.690
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:11.280
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.530
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:24.040
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:32.630
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:41.600
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.480
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.150
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.740
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.490
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.330
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.840
They say a vampire has turned up.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.050
Truly? How dreadful.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:24.890
Vampires were destroyed ages ago in a
battle with humankind, were they not?

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.560
Does that mean some survived?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.480
Have they risen once again
to visit vengeance upon us?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.230
Vampires are but a folktale.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.360
My great-grandfather claims
to have seen one.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.490
That's just another ghost story.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:42.990
No need to worry. The Church's
Chasseurs have sprung into action.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.000
I'm so cold.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:13.230
Are you sure you're well?
Shall I take you to the infirmary?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:18.280
No, I was simply feeling anemic.
There is no cause for concern.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.030
But you look quite pale.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:26.160
I'm going to see a doctor after this.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.170
That is the only one
I will allow to examine me.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:34.170
But thank you for your concern.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.590
Bad Murr!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.510
He's so warm.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.810
Um, my name is Amelia.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.850
Might I have an introduction?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.980
Sure! He is Murr.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.650
Please call him by that name.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.450
No, not <i>his </i>name...

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.700
Attention all passengers.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.910
La Baleine will be
arriving in Paris shortly.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:13.380
Please enjoy the rest of
your voyage through the sky.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.630
Paris!

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.390
Where's Paris, Mademoiselle Amelia?

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.560
I don't think we can see it yet.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.560
Oh, I see. How unfortunate.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.980
To think that such massive weight
could be made to fly...

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:42.150
The power of astermite
is truly awe inspiring.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.280
Is this your first time on an airship?

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.700
Yes.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.160
Will you see the sights of Paris?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.750
No, there is something I seek.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.620
You seek something?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.170
<i>The Book of Vanitas</i>.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.010
It's the name of the accursed grimoire

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:06.180
from the folktale,
"The Vampire of the Blue Moon."

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.890
You've not heard of it?

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.020
I lost track of time.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:18.400
We must prepare to disembark.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.240
I'm so very cold.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.410
You're really going through with this?

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.210
Naturally.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:40.920
For I know my target is
within this very airship.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.470
The ship's passenger facilities
are no longer available.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:48.600
Passengers who have not yet
prepared to disembark...

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.640
About what you said...

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:57.690
Do you truly believe that there is
such a thing as <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>?

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.270
I don't know.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:07.950
But I did receive a letter stating that
the book had been sighted in Paris.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.870
It was from my former teacher.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.130
Mon Chaton, my dearest kitten,

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:21.920
I wish for you to find
<i>The Book of Vanitas</i>

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.170
and assess its true nature.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:29.010
That is why I'm going to Paris.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.270
Mademoiselle! Are you not well?!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.190
Do not touch me!

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.990
Mademoiselle Amelia, your eyes are...

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.120
You're a... vampire.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.880
Now I have you!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.650
Well, I <i>thought </i>I had you.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.820
Who the devil are you?!

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.110
I could ask you the same.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.660
My business is with her alone.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.910
Here's some friendly advice.
Leave her and go.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.540
If you don't...

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:39.120
...you're in for a world of pain.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.130
I cannot do that.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.260
You move well despite
the woman in your arms!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.100
Damn it. What's he doing now?

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.360
A wire?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:39.060
Hey! Still alive, you quack?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.140
I'm not a quack!

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:52.490
I underestimated that crimson-eyed...

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.120
So he, too, is a vampire?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.990
Let's move.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:03.670
I'm cold. So cold. Cold, cold...

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:07.000
It's already too late.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.940
What a fine place. I like it.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:38.830
Will you give this place,
your true name, to me?

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.060
Mademoiselle Amelia!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.690
Get her to the infirmary.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.150
I'll apprehend them.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.860
No!

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.070
Mademoiselle?

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.340
Mademoiselle Amelia...

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:43.850
No... My strength is draining away.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:46.810
Let... go... of... me!

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:55.280
I no longer feel cold?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:04.410
I feel so warm. More! Give me more blood!

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.090
What's happening?!

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.260
Stop this!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.390
Mademoiselle!

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.470
You must know, don't you?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:28.810
We are forbidden from attacking humans.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:36.400
I can barely move.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.780
Could it be...

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.530
...poison?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.840
Bah, I did warn you that you
were in for a world of pain.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.220
The malady manifested as expected.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:01.680
Chills that are unbearable.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.850
Black tears that well forth
from the eyes and chest.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.350
And shadow briars.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:14.570
Your malnomen is Eglantine,
the Prison of Briars.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.490
Malnomen?

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:26.540
That is what we call the ruined remains of
a true name corrupted by the maladies.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.830
A vampire's true name is akin to
life itself, and hers was corrupted.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:36.210
As such, the urge to drink blood,
which is normally easy to suppress,

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.760
is now an irresistible force.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:43.550
Come on, you quack!
Cut the chit-chat and end it, already!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.800
Hold your horses, baldy!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.970
I'm not bald!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.150
Are you going to kill her?

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:56.190
Are you one of the Church's Chasseurs?

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:00.740
Or are you a bourreau,
an executioner here to slay her?

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:04.030
Me? A Chasseur? A bourreau?

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.160
That's a good one!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.830
<i>Non!</i>

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.630
I am a doctor, and
my specialty is vampires.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:19.590
I've come to cure her!

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:30.930
A cover of blue leather,
pages as black as night,

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:35.810
a clockwork grimoire
linked to a silver chain...

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.770
No, it can't be.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.860
The "Book of Vanitas"?!

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:52.620
Now then, shall we reclaim her true name?

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:12.850
The briars are disintegrating.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.370
Such warm light.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.170
It's like...

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.840
...spring sunshine.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.760
No.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:49.890
This light is your own.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:04.940
Florifel, she who guides spring!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:10.950
So, that <i>is </i>your true name.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.580
It truly suits you.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.250
My name...

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.210
My...

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:22.210
...true name!

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.130
Thank you!

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:38.600
Freeze!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.020
Hands in the air!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:43.360
You're the intruders who entered
through the observation gallery!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.440
Well, what do we do now?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:55.490
Here's some friendly advice.
Stay out of our way.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.290
If you don't, you're in for a world of--

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.920
Ow!

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.830
You fool!

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:30.900
The blue moon.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.580
I can see you're not afraid of it,

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:41.870
even though its blue light is said
to rob vampires of their power.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.790
It is a symbol of misfortune.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:52.720
But, teacher...

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:58.640
...in my eyes, that moon
is beautiful to behold.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:14.280
What in the world?!
I'm alive! I don't get it!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.830
But what's with this crummy landing?

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.080
What just happened?!

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:23.420
What did you do to her?!

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.840
A reverse operation.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:34.930
I used <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>
to remove the alteration formula,

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:38.510
i.e., the maladies
corrupting her true name.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.680
It was nothing.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.980
It was nothing?

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:47.480
How can you say that?

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.940
That was extraordinary!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.900
My teacher told me all about it!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.660
A true name is a vampire's life itself,

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:57.780
the constitutive formula
forming their existence!

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:00.870
It must never be taken by anyone else!

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.910
You reclaimed her name
for her, didn't you?!

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.290
That is extraordinary! Phenomenal!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:11.630
<i>The Book of Vanitas </i>is not some
accursed tome as told in folktales!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:18.970
I've never seen anyone look upon
this book with such stars in their eyes!

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:23.850
Did I say something funny?

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:28.940
That was hilarious. I like you.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.780
What's your name?

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:33.190
Noé.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.950
Noé? Child of the Ark, eh?

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.080
I am Vanitas!

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:47.040
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
passed on to me his name and his book.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.630
Yet I'm but a human!

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:53.380
Lend me your strength, Noé!

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.630
With your great fighting
ability and sturdy body,

00:19:56.630 --> 00:20:00.050
I've no doubt you'd make a fine shield!

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.510
That's a hard pass.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.890
I see, I see. So you'd be delighted!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:07.730
Wait.

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:10.610
Of course, you would say that!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:11.860
Excuse me.

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.360
Am I right?

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:19.950
There's been a surge in rampaging vampires
after maladies violated their true names.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:22.990
If nothing is done to find the root cause,

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:27.660
vampires will go extinct in
the not too distant future.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.590
I'll make sure that doesn't happen.

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:36.090
I will do as I please.

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:38.340
I will use the methods I choose.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.760
It matters not what you people want!

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.100
I <i>will </i>save the vampires.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:00.450
That was how it began.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.120
This is the tale of how I met Vanitas
and together wandered life's path.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.330
There was much we gained and much we lost.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.460
And then,

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:14.460
at the end of our journey...

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:24.600
...I would slay him by my own hand.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:29.050
In the Event of Rusty Hopes

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:01.820
I won't stop asking, Noé!

00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:03.820
Lend me your strength!

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:04.700
No.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:08.030
Why not?! What's the issue here?!

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:12.620
Just hear me out!
If you listen to all I've to say--

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:15.080
Come to think of it, I'm famished!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:19.960
Enough already. You truly are annoying.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:22.510
I can't take this anymore.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:27.220
We're here, Vanitas.

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:30.350
I'll go get Murr and my luggage--

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:32.140
How dumb can you be?!

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:35.230
Why would you return to the airship?!

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.770
There he is! The intruder!

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.400
Yikes! Not good!

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:42.110
Huh?

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:46.490
What the devil?!

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:52.070
In the City of Flowers
